The SDK fetches no model metadata and embeds no extract of it: a caller hands
in a models.dev document with catalog.WithMetadata
(docs/decisions/0093-MADR-take-model-metadata-from-the-caller.md). The module
does contain the following files of model data. The data originates from
models.dev (https://github.com/anomalyco/models.dev), which is licensed under
the MIT License:

  Copyright (c) 2025 models.dev

  llmprovider/internal/opencoderoute/routes_snapshot.json
    OpenCode's routes: the "opencode" and "opencode-go" sections of
    models.opencode.ai/api.json, retrieved 2026-09-27; embedded.
  llmprovider/catalog/testdata/ranking-2026-09-26/metadata.json
    a test fixture, trimmed from models.opencode.ai's document of 2026-09-26.
  llmprovider/catalog/testdata/ranking-2026-10-12/metadata.json
    a test fixture, the document's sections the SDK reads, recorded by
    internal/cmd/catalogs -snapshot on 2026-10-12.
  llmprovider/catalog/testdata/versions-2026-11-06/families.json
    a test fixture, from the models.dev document of 2026-11-06.
  llmprovider/catalog/testdata/metadata-0033/fixture.json
    a test fixture written in models.dev's format.
  llmprovider/catalog/testdata/extract-2026-10-12/api.json
    a test fixture: the limits extract the SDK embedded until 0093, dated
    2026-10-12, with OpenCode's routes, as a models.dev document.

Some of these files were taken from models.opencode.ai's copy of the models.dev
document, as their entries say.

The licence's full text is in LICENSE.models.dev.
